        "code": {
          "language": "plaintext",
          "showLineNumbers": false,
          "showMiniMap": false
        },
        "content": "### Appointment CloudFront edge \u2014 tb-dev (account 718959508124)\n\nCloudFront is a global service: **all `AWS/CloudFront` metrics are published in us-east-1 only**. Every query here overrides the datasource region to `us-east-1` (the `CloudWatch Logs \u2014 tb-dev01` datasource defaults to `eu-central-1`).\n\n**Panels that are expected to be empty until their prerequisite lands**\n\n- **Cache Hit Rate** and **Origin Latency** are CloudFront *additional* metrics. They do not exist until an `aws.cloudfront.MonitoringSubscription` is enabled on the distribution \u2014 the Pulumi half of https://github.com/thunderbird/platform-infrastructure/issues/826. Empty here means \"not subscribed\", not \"broken\".\n- **Every** panel needs `cloudwatch:GetMetricData` on the cross-account `mzla-tb-dev-grafana-cloudwatch` role, which today grants `logs:*` only. Same issue, same Pulumi half.\n- The distribution itself is created by https://github.com/thunderbird/platform-infrastructure/pull/844 (draft). Until it applies, the **Distribution** picker above is empty and every panel shows no data.\n\nCache hit rate is the success metric for this edge: a caching distribution that is not caching is a pure extra hop, i.e. a latency penalty. Read it **per cache behaviour** \u2014 the deliberately-uncached `/api/*` and `/fxa*` behaviours drag the distribution-wide aggregate below any naive \">90%\" target.",
        "mode": "markdown"
      },
      "title": "Prerequisites and how to read this dashboard",
      "type": "text"
    },
